    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) standing as our highest-projected start. His matchup against J. Irvin is ideal, as the combination of a favorable platoon edge (+14%) and the opportunity for stolen bases against a slow-working battery pushes his utility well into the elite tier. Joining him at the top of the lineup, **Junior Caminero** (75.53) remains a must-start; he benefits from an inviting park environment (+10%) and a favorable skill matchup against Barnett. We also see high-ceiling potential from **Yordan Alvarez** (69.53) and **Christian Yelich** (69.06), both of whom overcome neutral or slightly negative park factors through elite xwOBA or dynamic platoon advantages. **Trea Turner** (66.35) remains a cornerstone play, as the matchup against Pallante provides a rare combination of favorable SP skill and a slow delivery, maximizing his elite stolen base potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Carson Benge** (52.26) from the active lineup. While **Carson Benge** brings strong SP skill advantages against M. P\u00e9rez, his projected floor was ultimately undercut by a negative platoon penalty for left-on-left matchups, keeping him behind the higher-scoring profiles of **Nelson Velazquez** (59.77) and **Kyle Schwarber** (62.84). We continue to monitor **Casey Schmitt**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** are currently excluded due to rest or lack of confirmed lineup presence.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly regarding **Caleb Durbin** (43.26). His score is heavily suppressed by a grueling matchup against Cease (-19% SP Skill), placing him at the bottom of our active rotation. We are operating with a cautious approach to **Dillon Dingler** (47.75) as well, whose efficiency is capped by a difficult platoon against Bibee. While we are currently fielding our optimal lineup based on ATC projections, be aware that any late-day weather shifts in these respective venues could necessitate a quick pivot to our depth reserves, though no immediate meteorological threats are currently flagged for the Zebras.",
